{"title":"Stat2 Python Notes","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Stat2 Python Notes","subtitle":"Statistics translated into working marimo notebooks","abstract":"A browsable collection of rendered Python marimo notes migrated from the Stat2 Julia examples."},"headingText":"Start with a question","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n<div class=\"home-hero\">\n<p class=\"home-kicker\">STAT2 / PYTHON BRANCH / MARIMO NOTES</p>\n<p class=\"home-lede\">A working archive of statistical ideas, carried from Julia into inspectable Python notebooks.</p>\n<div class=\"home-actions\"><a class=\"home-button home-button-primary\" href=\"notes.html\">Browse the notebook library</a><a class=\"home-button\" href=\"MIGRATION.html\">Read the migration guide</a></div>\n</div>\n\nThis site presents the migrated notes as static marimo HTML pages. The notebooks remain runnable locally with the `lock5stat-env` conda environment.\n\n::: {.callout-note}\nRead the result in the browser, then open the source notebook when you want to run or edit it.\n:::\n\n<div class=\"method-strip\">\n<div><span class=\"method-number\">01</span><strong>Load</strong><br>Polars data frames</div>\n<div><span class=\"method-number\">02</span><strong>Explore</strong><br>Great Tables summaries</div>\n<div><span class=\"method-number\">03</span><strong>Model</strong><br>SciPy and statsmodels</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"note-links\">\n<a href=\"notes/UnitB-Anova/ch05/p540-rat-fat.html\"><span>ANOVA</span><strong>Rat fat experiment</strong><small>Compare high-protein diet sources</small></a>\n<a href=\"notes/UnitA-LinearRegression/ch02/bookpages-price-reg.html\"><span>LINEAR REGRESSION</span><strong>Book pages and price</strong><small>Open a model close to the data</small></a>\n<a href=\"notes/UnitD-Timeseries/ch12/p1446-cpi-arima-model.html\"><span>TIME SERIES</span><strong>CPI and ARIMA</strong><small>Inspect a seasonal workflow</small></a>\n</div>\n\n## Built to stay close to the data\n\nThe Python notes use Polars for tabular data, Great Tables for exploratory summaries, and SciPy or statsmodels for statistical models where the Julia analysis has been translated.\n\nSee the [migration guide](MIGRATION.html) for coverage and environment details.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n<div class=\"home-hero\">\n<p class=\"home-kicker\">STAT2 / PYTHON BRANCH / MARIMO NOTES</p>\n<p class=\"home-lede\">A working archive of statistical ideas, carried from Julia into inspectable Python notebooks.</p>\n<div class=\"home-actions\"><a class=\"home-button home-button-primary\" href=\"notes.html\">Browse the notebook library</a><a class=\"home-button\" href=\"MIGRATION.html\">Read the migration guide</a></div>\n</div>\n\nThis site presents the migrated notes as static marimo HTML pages. The notebooks remain runnable locally with the `lock5stat-env` conda environment.\n\n::: {.callout-note}\nRead the result in the browser, then open the source notebook when you want to run or edit it.\n:::\n\n<div class=\"method-strip\">\n<div><span class=\"method-number\">01</span><strong>Load</strong><br>Polars data frames</div>\n<div><span class=\"method-number\">02</span><strong>Explore</strong><br>Great Tables summaries</div>\n<div><span class=\"method-number\">03</span><strong>Model</strong><br>SciPy and statsmodels</div>\n</div>\n\n## Start with a question\n\n<div class=\"note-links\">\n<a href=\"notes/UnitB-Anova/ch05/p540-rat-fat.html\"><span>ANOVA</span><strong>Rat fat experiment</strong><small>Compare high-protein diet sources</small></a>\n<a href=\"notes/UnitA-LinearRegression/ch02/bookpages-price-reg.html\"><span>LINEAR REGRESSION</span><strong>Book pages and price</strong><small>Open a model close to the data</small></a>\n<a href=\"notes/UnitD-Timeseries/ch12/p1446-cpi-arima-model.html\"><span>TIME SERIES</span><strong>CPI and ARIMA</strong><small>Inspect a seasonal workflow</small></a>\n</div>\n\n## Built to stay close to the data\n\nThe Python notes use Polars for tabular data, Great Tables for exploratory summaries, and SciPy or statsmodels for statistical models where the Julia analysis has been translated.\n\nSee the [migration guide](MIGRATION.html) for coverage and environment details.\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":true,"code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":true,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["styles.css"],"toc":true,"output-file":"index.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","source-notebooks-prefix":"Source","other-links-title":"Other Links","code-links-title":"Code Links","launch-dev-container-title":"Launch Dev Container","launch-binder-title":"Launch Binder","article-notebook-label":"Arti